# =========================
# Windows detritus
# =========================

# Windows image file caches
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db

# Folder config file
Desktop.ini

# Recycle Bin used on file shares
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Mac desktop service store files
.DS_Store

_NCrunch*
# Resources/ is where the corpus lives: about a gigabyte of third-party Bibles, lexicons and
# alignments. It is not this repository's to carry -- the fetch scripts under scripts/ and the
# sources they name put it there, and Dataset:ResourcesPath can point somewhere else entirely.
#
# The three rules below re-admit, in order: every folder, so git looks inside; nothing that is in
# one; and then the two kinds of file a fresh clone is useless without. Do not simplify the middle
# rule away -- without it the negations above match everything and a stray `git add` commits a
# gigabyte.
Resources/*
!Resources/*/
Resources/*/*

# What each corpus folder is, so a copy of the data can be checked against the one this
# repository's measurements were taken from. Thirteen of the seventeen folders have no fetch script
# and exist because somebody downloaded them once; without this, two machines can disagree about the
# bytes under one folder name and every number either measured is unfalsifiable. 4 KB.
!Resources/MANIFEST.json

# The licence beside each corpus folder. A licence statement that survives only on the machine
# that fetched the data is not a record anybody can check, which is the entire reason for keeping
# a copy next to the bytes. Kilobytes; the data they describe stays out.
!Resources/*/LICENCE.md

# The world history this project fetched itself: three CC0 Wikidata exports, the SPARQL queries
# that produced them, and a README recording when they were run. 319 KB, and without them the
# world layer loads nothing and its test fails on every clean checkout while passing on the
# machine that did the fetching.
!Resources/WorldHistory/**

# JetBrains IDE settings
.idea/

# The database password reaches compose through this file, and it is not this repository's to carry.
.env
